Citation Style Language styles and locales

Scient includes unmodified CSL style files from the Citation Style Language styles
repository (https://github.com/citation-style-language/styles) and an unmodified CSL
locale file from the CSL locales repository
(https://github.com/citation-style-language/locales). Styles a person downloads in
Scient come from the same repository through the Zotero Style Repository
(https://www.zotero.org/styles).

This software uses CSL styles and locales from the Citation Style Language project:
https://citationstyles.org/

The styles and locales are released under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
3.0 Unported license: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/
Their author, contributor and translator listings are kept as they are, in each file's
metadata.

Bundled styles (styles repository commit 7a37c5a736c10fbd468bc31f92cbc6eafaa2173d):
apa, chicago-author-date, chicago-notes-bibliography, harvard-cite-them-right, ieee,
nature, science, cell, american-medical-association, modern-language-association,
american-chemical-society, nlm-citation-sequence, elsevier-vancouver, bmj, the-lancet,
the-new-england-journal-of-medicine, pnas, plos, elsevier-harvard,
springer-basic-author-date.

